          "info": {
            "name": "Get Contracts By Registry",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "https://api.myaltimate.com/registries/:registry_id/contracts/",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "registry_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "token": "{{bearerToken}}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Fetches all the contracts for a tenant in a registry.\nparam db: The database session for accessing the database and the tenant schema.\nparam registry: The registry the contract is being fetched from\nparam auth: The authorization token for the request.\nreturn: A dictionary containing all the contracts"
        },
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "Create Contract In Registry",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": "https://api.myaltimate.com/registries/:registry_id/contracts/",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "registry_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "type": "json",
              "data": "{}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "token": "{{bearerToken}}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Create a contract in the registry and database.\n1. Checks if the contract already exists in the registry.\n2. Validates the contract. If invalid, raise exception\n3. If it does not exist, creates the contract in the registry.\n4. If it exists and is same do nothing. Else create a new version.\n\n\n:param db: The database session for accessing the database.\n:param contract_request: The contract creation request containing the contract definition and other metadata.\n:param tenant: The tenant object for "
        },
